---
/**
 * V3 /book closed-state acknowledgment card. Two flavors:
 *
 *   - 'booked'   — replaces the chat after the prospect confirms a slot.
 *                  Shows the confirmed time and (optional) Google Meet
 *                  link / reschedule link.
 *
 *   - 'done'     — replaces the chat after the prospect clicks Done.
 *                  Short acknowledgment line. The only affordance is the
 *                  primary "Pick a time to talk" CTA.
 *
 * Pre-rendered hidden; book.ts reveals the appropriate flavor via
 * data-flavor attribute and populates fields (slot text, meet link).
 *
 * Per the no-fabricated-content policy: the Done card MUST NOT promise
 * follow-up outreach. Tests/forbidden-strings.test.ts blocks regression
 * patterns scoped to this file.
 */
---

<section id="intake-closed" class="ss-closed" hidden>
  <!-- Booked flavor -->
  <div id="closed-booked" class="ss-closed-card" hidden data-flavor="booked">
    <p class="ss-eyebrow">Confirmed</p>
    <p id="closed-booked-slot" class="ss-headline-sm"></p>
    <div id="closed-booked-meet-row" class="ss-stack" hidden>
      <a id="closed-booked-meet-link" href="#" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="ss-link">
        Join the call
      </a>
    </div>
    <div id="closed-booked-manage-row" class="ss-stack" hidden>
      <a id="closed-booked-manage-link" href="#" class="ss-quiet-link"> Reschedule or cancel </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!--
    Done flavor. Copy authored by Captain — placeholder lives in the
    component for now. Forbidden-strings test scopes regression
    patterns ("we'll", "we will", "review your", "get back",
    "in touch") to this component to prevent fabricated follow-up
    promises from sneaking in.
  -->
  <div id="closed-done" class="ss-closed-card" hidden data-flavor="done">
    <p class="ss-eyebrow">Got it</p>
    <p class="ss-headline-sm">Thanks for sharing.</p>
    <a href="#" id="closed-done-pick-time" class="ss-primary mt-stack"> Pick a time to talk </a>
  </div>
</section>
